    "description": "<h3>What it is</h3><p>A compounded injectable that combines two active ingredients in a single vial: tirzepatide, the dual GLP-1 and GIP receptor agonist used in modern weight management protocols, and NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide), a coenzyme central to mitochondrial energy production. Each 5mL vial contains 20mg/mL of tirzepatide (100mg total) and 200mg/mL of NAD+ (1,000mg total).</p><h3>Why pair them</h3><p>Tirzepatide drives weight loss through appetite suppression, slowed gastric emptying, and improved insulin sensitivity. In published SURMOUNT clinical trials at 15mg, participants saw an average of ~20.9% body weight reduction over 72 weeks. The flip side is that aggressive caloric reduction often comes with fatigue, brain fog, and low energy, the side effects most weight loss patients describe as the hardest part of the protocol.</p><p>NAD+ is a coenzyme required for nearly every energy-producing reaction in the cell. Levels naturally decline with age and under metabolic stress. Pairing supplemental NAD+ with tirzepatide is intended to support sustained energy and cellular function while the body is in a caloric deficit, giving patients an easier subjective experience through the harder weeks of titration.</p><h3>How it's used</h3><p>Subcutaneous injection, once weekly. Most protocols start at a low tirzepatide dose (typically 2.5mg per week) and titrate up every four weeks as tolerance allows. Always work with a licensed healthcare provider to determine the right starting dose, titration schedule, and protocol length for your situation.</p><h3>Quality and sourcing</h3><p>Compounded in the USA by our licensed pharmacy partner under USP 797 sterile compounding standards. Third-party tested for potency, sterility, and endotoxin before any vial ships. Manufactured fresh to order, not pulled from warehouse inventory.</p><h3>Important</h3><p>For research and educational purposes only. Compounded medications are not FDA-approved drugs. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. Discuss with a licensed healthcare provider before beginning any peptide protocol. Must be 18 years or older to purchase.</p>",
